th.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:19:43-08:00","id":1193215,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna revive this thread because the Beast Player's Guide has given us new Hungers and Families, and thus created the potential for this superhero/supervillain duo:<br /> <br /> <b>Talassii Nemesis -- </b>the Fear of Captivity (but emphatically not killing or torturing their captives) + the Hunger for Punishment.<br /> <br /> versus<br /> <br /> <b>Inguma Enabler -- </b>the Fear of the Other (like, I dunno, <i>clowns)</i> + the Hunger for Transgressions, aka getting people to do things they know to be wrong. Basically this combo yields Heath Ledger Joker with body horror turned up to 9000.<br /> <br /> The Enabler is trying to increase their power/influence (and perhaps purse the Inheritance) by ramping up the scale of the transgressions they engineer....and the Nemesis keeps chasing along behind yelling &quot;Caaaaaarl, that kiiiillls people!&quot; and trying to envelope the Enabler in spiders.<br /> <br /> (I am v. much enjoying this book.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"